config CHIRUNO_SMART_SWAPPINESS
	bool "Chiruno Kernel smart swappiness support"
	default n
	help
	  This option enables a swappiness controller for Android 5.15 GKI
	  kernels. It monitors available memory once per second. When memory
	  pressure is detected, it lowers vm_swappiness and the swappiness of
	  every memory cgroup. When the pressure clears, it restores the
	  boot-time swappiness value.

	  The controller is enabled by default only on devices in the 8 GiB RAM
	  range. On other devices it remains disabled at boot and can be enabled
	  through /proc/chiruno_swappiness/smart_swappiness.

	  Say Y here to compile this controller directly into the kernel.
